## Summary
Stalled real estate project financing (PF) sites in South Korea are set to be converted into purchase-rental housing for young adults and newlyweds. This initiative aims to address housing shortages and revitalize unused real estate projects.

## Key Points
- Conversion of stopped real estate PF projects into rental housing units.
- Target beneficiaries are youth and newly married couples to provide affordable housing options.
- The new housing model combines purchase and rental elements.
- Potential to stimulate the real estate market and support social welfare policies.


